{#
  Mu DevOps Dependency Version Control

  =====================================================================================================================
  About
  =====================================================================================================================
  This file centralizes definitions of versions placed into files synced from Mu DevOps to other repos before the
  files are synced.

  =====================================================================================================================
  `mu_devops` / `mu_devops_sha` Example:
  =====================================================================================================================
  `mu_devops` defines the git tag value of Mu DevOps that will be synced (via file sync) to repos that depend on this
  repo. `mu_devops_sha` is the full commit SHA that tag points to. Synced workflow files pin the `uses:`
  reusable-workflow ref to `mu_devops_sha` (with `mu_devops` kept as a trailing `# vX.Y.Z` comment), so that
  leaf repos are not affected by a tag being moved or deleted.

  Example flow:
    1. Make a new Mu DevOps release (e.g. "v1.0.0")
    2. Look up the commit SHA that the "v1.0.0" tag points to (e.g. `git rev-parse v1.0.0`, or the commit shown on
       the release/tag page in GitHub)
    3. Update this file to set `mu_devops` to "v1.0.0" and `mu_devops_sha` to the resolved commit SHA

  Step (3) causes the following automated actions to take place after the change is merged:
    1. All sync files (e.g. an Azure Pipeline file) that depend on this version get the new values substituted
    2. All sync files with the substituted values are synced to their respective repos (PRs created with the change)
    3. After the PRs in those repos are merged, they use the new version of Mu DevOps

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Note: This file is not actually synced. It controls the version used in other files that are synced.

  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
#}

